;. /task_learning_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition task_learning
  ;= Learn from a completed task

    Invoke this after a task, or attach it to deliberately selected evidence.
    Inspect the settled native work record using Declared authoring actions,
    Inspect callable definitions. Set inspection care x for its own record, not a
    subtree. Bind capture to the raw inspection cell path, without /x. The cell
    retains the original typed work. A running task is refused.

    Bind sources to a collection named task and instructions. The catalogue
    supplies an explicitly labelled sample; replace those bindings with the
    actual task and current instructions before applying a lesson to your work.
    Select the Nenex writer, a new destination and a provider, or revise manually.
    This flow proposes improvements. It never changes instructions, publishes a
    new executable procedure, or installs an after-task hook automatically.

    ;@ /flow/input capture
    ;= Selected settled native work in an ordinary frozen cell

    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Task goal and existing instructions as captured source evidence

    ;@ /flow/step grounded ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/library/task_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind capture capture
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Check settled work and retain its exact native evidence

    ;@ /flow/step lessons ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/revise
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Propose supported lessons through the ordinary revision hand

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages lessons
    ;@ /flow/bind sources grounded
    ;= Keep lesson documents and compact provenance together

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Guarded publication of proposals

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses native task instructions
    ;= What this task taught us
      Compare the explicit goal, retained outcome and current instructions.
      Explain one concrete success or failure supported by the captured record.
      Distinguish observation, interpretation and a proposed reusable rule.
      Cite the exact native reference. A bounded reflected display is not a full
      execution trace; do not invent omitted actions, timings or test outcomes.
      If the record cannot establish a lesson, return empty source with the gap.

    ;@ /flow/page proposed_instruction
    ;@ /flow/uses native task instructions
    ;= A proposed instruction change
      Propose a small actionable change to the supplied instructions, with the
      triggering condition, concrete action, evidence and counterexample. Explain
      when the rule should not apply. Label it a proposal requiring deliberate
      adoption. Do not claim this flow changed anyone's instructions or memory.

    ;@ /flow/page reusable_procedure
    ;@ /flow/uses native task instructions
    ;= Turn the lesson into a reusable flow
      Describe explicit inputs, deterministic checks, judgment boundaries, result
      and guarded effects for a possible reusable procedure. Put any illustrative
      Semidoc in an inert literal block. Use existing retained-run or investigation
      extraction and callable composition to author an executable procedure;
      this prose proposal is not a published flow. Name missing evidence as a gap.
